## Scientific reconstruction

1. The full-space gap proof is valid as written. The prefix-only telescoping
   identity for a word of adjacent swaps is exact. Cauchy--Schwarz and the
   repeated-edge count yield the conservative transposition comparison.
   Summing its edge coefficients gives 2N k(N-k)<=N^3/2. On N spin-half
   factors, the complete-graph exchange operator is N(N+2)I/4-S^2; its
   complement to the unique maximum-spin symmetric representation has
   eigenvalue at least N. Combining gives gamma_N=2 J_F/N^2 on the whole
   source Hilbert space, including its many-excitation sectors. No one-head
   surrogate is used.
2. With the stated decoupled old qubit, F=H+omega N_A commutes exactly with
   L_F and A=2rV+zZ_p. Direct multiplication of Z=P-q R_F QAP gives the
   q^2(X A_P-A X) residual. Norms of the two bare/corrected endpoints are
   both charged, giving 6q/gamma_N+18tq^2/gamma_N. There is no assumption
   that the prepared state is dressed or that qT is small.
3. On the equatorial source product, the source operators' deviations create
   the orthogonal sum of N one-spin-flipped product vectors. With the specified
   raising/lowering convention, the old residual is sigma_+-sigma_- of norm
   one. Its complete isometry norm is exactly r/sqrt(N). This gives a bound
   retaining every source output, rather than only a reduced old channel.
4. The phase sign is consistent: exp(-i omega n T) conjugates the rotation
   axis from phi to phi-omega T. Thus phi=phi0+omega T produces the target
   in the order W exp(-iTH), with the explicit exp[-i theta0] comparison
   factor. The source field motion remains in the output vector. The scalar
   reserve R and full normalized scalar s_K are different valid ledgers.
5. Each of the three terms in the source's isometry error is <=epsilon/8
   under its choices. The conversion to unhalved trace distance plus the
   single state and generator allowances totals epsilon. N=O(epsilon^-2),
   gamma_N^-1=O(epsilon^-4), and T=O(epsilon^-5) follow for fixed nonzero
   theta. Every added local identity reserve is present in the stated common
   incident norm bound; total norm and total energy need not stay bounded.

## Qualifications for any publication

- This is one controlled old qubit, possibly with genuinely decoupled retained
  spectators. The general coupled-plant theorem remains open. The augmented
  polynomial Lie certificate does not imply the exact resonance used here.
- The source state, phase calculation after selecting T, actual isolation and
  precision are supplied. No preparation or source-selection law follows.
  The whole-state preparation allowance includes any correlation with old
  factors and uses their exact unconditional marginal.
- The mathematical minimal ceiling in the source is an existence choice. A
  uniformly terminating implementation for arbitrary computable target angles
  should use a strict rational upper margin, rather than deciding whether a
  computable real equals an integer. For rational epsilon, a simple replacement
  is N=max(2,ceil[(40/epsilon)^2]), since 1+theta<5. It preserves all three
  error estimates and powers. If a is the minimum of the source's two
  positive upper constraints, choose a rational q with a/2<q<a by certified
  interval refinement. The constant-factor lower bound preserves the runtime
  power; an arbitrarily smaller q would not. This avoids deciding an exact
  comparison of real inputs. Do not silently replace the original frozen
  choice or claim the old exact minimal choice was an executed algorithm.
- The scalar target is handled separately as free old evolution, not by
  dividing by theta or q. The r=0 and either sign of omega cases are included
  in the non-scalar proof. Additional fixed-target timing or preparation
  switching errors need a resplit allowance.
- Section 8's finite Sylvester/corrector implication has the displayed exact
  algebra and explicitly supplied spectral/projector data. It does not
  independently construct those data in the generic setting. Sections 9--10
  are uncompleted architecture proposals and a diagnostic for a sufficient
  clock recipe. They are not accepted as a general physical realization or
  an impossibility theorem.

## Evidence assessment so far

The complete author check source independently assembles physical finite
matrices, with nonzero/negative frequencies and a pure-Z example. Its
corrector, fluctuation, scalar and isometry comparisons are substantive finite
checks, not an implementation of the asymptotic recipe. The full claimed
scope still rests on the analytic argument. Root has read the implementation
but has not yet independently verified its recorded streams/freeze or run
discriminating mutations. No accepted scientific status is declared here.

Root's separate fixed-slew candidate does not imply this static construction;
it uses externally supplied timing and a different qualitative compiler. The
two routes may coexist but their resource formulas must not be mixed.
